<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulugh Beg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1449</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ulugh Beg was a Timurid ruler and astronomer, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>, who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> for decades and died in 1449. He built a great observatory and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasa</a> in Samarkand and sponsored astronomical tables of remarkable accuracy. His brief reign as supreme ruler ended with his overthrow and death at the instigation of his son.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulugh-beg.jpg" alt="Ulugh Beg" width="314" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ulugh_Beg,_Timurid_painting_1425-50.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
